        <headline>Flood Watch issued September 24 at 11:44AM CDT until September 25 at 7:00AM CDT by NWS Amarillo TX</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be
possible.

* WHERE...Portions of the Panhandle of Oklahoma, including the
following counties, Cimarron and Texas and the Panhandle of Texas,
including the following counties, Dallam, Hartley and Sherman.

* WHEN...Through Friday morning.

* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,
creeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- Heavy rainfall of 2-4" over the last 24 hours has fallen over the
area. Additional rainfall over saturated grounds could lead to
run-off and flooding concerns.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood
Warnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared
to take action should flooding develop.</instruction>
